{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103102-exceptional-successes-and-arcane-conditions","id":1103102,"title":"Exceptional Successes and Arcane Conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-13T06:17:48-07:00","id":1103102,"title":"Exceptional Successes and Arcane Conditions","content":"One of the options for an exceptional success on a spellcasting roll is a &quot;Condition which grants arcane beats when resolved&quot;. This has proven a fairly popular option among the players in my current game (we're using shared beats so there's a teamwork incentive to taking the condition especially) but the book doesn't give any examples of what these kind of conditions might look like.<br /> <br /> I'm currently stuck trying to come up with a condition to give an Acanthus for an exceptional success on a post-cog, but there have been, and will be, other spells needing other conditions.<br /> <br /> What have people done with this mechanic? Do you have any advice on how you develop these kinds of conditions or examples of the kinds of conditions you've created?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5958-logocentric","name":"Logocentric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T06:21:58-07:00","id":1103105,"title":"","content":"I tend to either just use Conditions that are in the book, or to mix and match bits of different Conditions for what I want. When I'm stumped though, I just give the Arcane Beat and skip the Comdition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T06:44:19-07:00","id":1103111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logocentric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103102-exceptional-successes-and-arcane-conditions#post1103102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the options for an exceptional success on a spellcasting roll is a &quot;Condition which grants arcane beats when resolved&quot;. This has proven a fairly popular option among the players in my current game (we're using shared beats so there's a teamwork incentive to taking the condition especially) but the book doesn't give any examples of what these kind of conditions might look like.<br /> <br /> I'm currently stuck trying to come up with a condition to give an Acanthus for an exceptional success on a post-cog, but there have been, and will be, other spells needing other conditions.<br /> <br /> What have people done with this mechanic? Do you have any advice on how you develop these kinds of conditions or examples of the kinds of conditions you've created?</div> </div> </div> </div>While not specifically called Arcane conditions, dont most players do this so they can get Inspired or Steadfast? Ive not had a chance to play or run 2e but those are the conditions that id fish for with praxis and ES.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T06:46:21-07:00","id":1103112,"title":"","content":"We have about 20 of these written up so far. I'll post them later today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T09:09:35-07:00","id":1103156,"title":"","content":"That would be FANTASTIC. We really need those. Inspired, Steadfast and Informed are getting old and we've only played two sessions in my new chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T11:25:27-07:00","id":1103221,"title":"","content":"Here are the ones I have. There are more we've used on the fly but we didn't write them down, since they were highly situational (not just bonuses to casting in one form or another). I'll try to remember.<br /> <br /> <b>Steadfast Casting</b> - Resolve this Condition to turn a failed spellcasting roll into a success. This does not function on a dramatic failure, though you may resolve it before rolling a Chance Die to roll a single regular die instead.<br /> <b>Inspired Imago</b> - Resolve this Condition to achieve an exceptional casting success with three dice instead of five. You may not choose to gain a Condition in return for your exceptional success, though the other options are still valid<br /> <br /> <b>Stable Imago</b> - Resolve this Condition to use as a Yantra that functions as a Dedicated Tool for the purposes of Paradox (Reducing Paradox by two dice)<br /> <b>Reckless Sorcery</b> - Resolve this Condition to use as a Yantra that provides a +2 Bonus. Increase Paradox Dice for the spell by 1.<br /> <b>Fickle Imago</b> - Resolve this Condition before rolling for spellcasting. A success on the roll is treated as an exceptional success. A failure is treated as a Dramatic Failure. If you achieve an exceptional success, you may not choose to gain a Condition as a result, though the other options are still valid.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Magic</b> - Resolve this Condition to use as a Yantra worth a bonus equal to your dots in Death on a non-Death spell that is semiotically compatible.<br /> <b>Weaver's Imago</b> - Resolve this Condition to use as a Yantra worth a bonus equal to your dots in Fate on a non-Fate spell that is semiotically compatible.<br /> <b>Brilliant Sorcery</b> - Resolve this Condition to use as a Yantra worth a bonus equal to your dots in Forces on a non-Forces spell that is semiotically compatible.<br /> <b>Primal Channel</b> - Resolve this Condition to use as a Yantra worth a bonus equal to your dots in Life on a non-Life spell that is semiotically compatible.<br /> <b>Fortified Magic</b> - Resolve this Condition to use as a Yantra worth a bonus equal to your dots in Matter on a non-Matter spell that is semiotically compatible.<br /> <b>Warlock's Right</b> - Resolve this Condition to use as a Yantra worth a bonus equal to your dots in Mind on a non-Mind spell that is semiotically compatible.<br /> <b>Supernal Sorcery</b> - Resolve this Condition to use as a Yantra worth a bonus equal to your dots in Prime on a non-Prime spell that is semiotically compatible.<br /> <b>Sympathetic Imago</b> - Resolve this Condition to use as a Yantra worth a bonus equal to your dots in Space on a non-Space spell that is semiotically compatible.<br /> <b>Animist's Aura </b>- Resolve this Condition to use as a Yantra worth a bonus equal to your dots in Spirit on a non-Spirit spell that is semiotically compatible.<br /> <b>Eternal Magic</b> - Resolve this Condition to use as a Yantra worth a bonus equal to your dots in Time on a non-Time spell that is semiotically compatible.<br /> <br /> <b>Place of Power</b> - Resolve this Condition to double the bonus from all Place Yantras for the rest of the scene.<br /> <b>Ritualist's Art</b> - Resolve this Condition to raise the cap on bonus gained from Ritual Magic from +5 to +10 for one spell cast. You must still spend the appropriate number of extra intervals casting to reach the new cap.<br /> <b>Mana Sacrament</b> - Resolve this Condition and spend 1, 3, or 5 Mana to use it as a Sacrament. 1 Point of Mana is a +1 Sacrament, 3 Points is a +2 Sacrament, and 5 Points is a +3 Sacrament.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 06-16-2017, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T18:38:56-07:00","id":1103351,"title":"","content":"Very cool, hadnt thought of using conditions as Yantra's. Its not in the books though is it? I like it and would use it, just wanting to make sure its not one of the things ive missed in 2e..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T02:48:02-07:00","id":1103426,"title":"","content":"It is not. Conditions are designed to be mini self-contained rulesets, so it seemed appropriate.<br /> You can skip the 'Yantra' part and just apply the bonuses as a flat boost, but that makes everything significantly more powerful so I'd cut the strength of the bonus in half (round up). <br /> <br /> I made them Yantras because we don't let non-Yantra bonuses factor into the dice pool for purposes of determining spell factors in our games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T13:26:08-07:00","id":1103595,"title":"","content":"What do you mean by semiotically compatible? Like for say, Shadow magic. Could you give an example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T03:15:23-07:00","id":1103756,"title":"","content":"First thing that comes to mind is a Forces spell to shut down all the lights in an area, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T04:29:13-07:00","id":1103764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103102-exceptional-successes-and-arcane-conditions?p=1103595#post1103595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by semiotically compatible? Like for say, Shadow magic. Could you give an example.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103102-exceptional-successes-and-arcane-conditions?p=1103756#post1103756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First thing that comes to mind is a Forces spell to shut down all the lights in an area, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, exactly this. Or, for example: using<br /> <br /> 1) Brilliant Sorcery to help you control a Fire Spirit<br /> 2) Primal Channel to aid with a Mind Spell that causes someone to give in to their basic instincts<br /> 3) Fortified Magic to aid in a Spirit Spell that causes a car to malfunction (Gremlins)<br /> 4) Supernal Sorcery on a Mind spell to force someone to tell the truth<br /> <br /> You're looking for a thematic connection between the spell you're doing and the Arcana you want to add as a Yantra. It doesn't have to be something you can <i>do</i> with the Conditioned Arcana (though that's easiest) just something that's <i>related </i>conceptually<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T10:43:45-07:00","id":1103859,"title":"","content":"I like it. It's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T11:32:18-07:00","id":1106170,"title":"","content":"Inodiv's response is very cool, and something I'm likely to nick.<br /> I tend to award fairly generic conditions along the lines of (examples from actual play):<br /> <br /> +2 to do (some subset of a skill) until you fail.<br /> (Okay, you blazed that influence electricity roll. Take the electrician trait for +2 to work out or work with wiring until you fail.)<br /> <br /> Resolve this to automatically succeed at one relevant task<br /> (Okay, you smashed your occult roll to know about the White Lily society. Resolve this condition to just <i>happen</i> to know something else about a member you meet.)<br /> <br /> The ST can resolve this to give you some intuition or hint<br /> (&quot;Okay, so suddenly that scene didn't happen. Rewind to just as you met your target - &quot; &quot;Hey, wait a second, I have the time traveller condition&quot; &quot;Huh. So you do. Cool. Someone is fucking with your timeline.&quot; &quot;Group-hug shield of chronos!&quot;)<br /> <br /> Or a Condition from the book of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}